  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_type\": \"CEFR Englis_Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn the bustling city of New York, a new trend is taking root: the 'couchsurfing' movement. This unique approach to travel involves meeting locals and staying with them for free or at minimal cost. The idea was born out of necessity; many young people cannot afford hotel rooms, so they turned to online forums to find hosts willing to share their homes. Today, the movement has grown into a global phenomenon with millions of participants worldwide.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main topic of this passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"The history of hotels in New York.\",\n        \"A description of a typical couchsurfing experience.\",\n        \"The economic impact of the 'couchsurfing' movement on local businesses.\",\n        \"A comparison between traditional accommodation and couchsurfing.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"The economic impact of the 'couchsurfing' movement on local businesses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"Why did people start using couchsurfing?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Because they wanted to save money on travel expenses.\",\n        \"To find a more sustainable way of living in cities.\",\n        \"For the social benefits and cultural immersion it provides.\",\n        \"As an alternative to traditional accommodation for those who dislike hotels.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"Because they wanted to save money on travel expenses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the term 'couchsurfing' refer to?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"The practice of using a couch as your primary form of transportation.\",\n        \"A type of accommodation where you sleep on someone's sofa in exchange for help with household chores.\",\n        \"The act of surfing the internet to find hosts willing to let you stay at their home.\",\n        \"A social network where people can share information about free accommodation in exchange for help with household chores.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"The act of surfing the internet to find hosts willing to let you stay at their home.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the growth of couchsurfing?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It has remained a small-scale phenomenon with limited impact.\",\n        \"The movement is now primarily focused on providing free accommodation for tourists only.\",\n        \"It has become a global phenomenon with millions of participants worldwide.\",\n        \"The number of couchsurfers is declining due to increased competition from hotel chains.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It has become a global phenomenon with millions of participants worldwide.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"How does the author express their attitude towards couchsurfing?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"They are skeptical and question its sustainability.\",\n        \"They view it as a necessary evolution in travel accommodations.\",\n        \"They express concern about the impact on local businesses.\",\n        \"They emphasize its potential to promote cultural understanding and international friendships.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"They view it as a necessary evolution in travel accommodations.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
